.nh
.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-features-update - Update a feature


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago features update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint updates an existing feature representing an entitlement component of your application. Only the fields present in the payload are updated. Privileges are matched by their code, an unknown code adds a new privilege and a known one updates its name and adds the select options of the payload to the existing ones. The value type of an existing privilege cannot be changed. Privileges left out of the payload are kept, use the delete privilege endpoint to remove one.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--description\fP=""
	Internal description of the feature.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Name of the feature.

.PP
\fB--privileges\fP=""
	Privileges associated with this feature. Can be empty.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago features update <code> --input @payload.json
  lago features update <code> --input @payload.json --output json  # full resource
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlago-features(1)\fP
